{"id":"tam-t0-0001","lang":"tam","tier":0,"slot":"greeting.hello","domain":1,"text_native":"வணக்கம்","text_romanized":"vuh-nnuhk-kuhm","text_english":"Hello.","source_caption":"Hello.","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"The default greeting anywhere. Works with every age and every status.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Tamil phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Tamil","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"tam-t0-0002","lang":"tam","tier":0,"slot":"greeting.how-are-you","domain":1,"text_native":"எப்படி இருக்கீங்க?","text_romanized":"ehp-puh-dih ih-ruk-keeng-guh?","text_english":"How are you?","source_caption":"How are you?","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"The opening move in almost every conversation. In most of these languages it is a greeting rather than a question and does not expect a literal answer.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Tamil phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Tamil","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"tam-t0-0003","lang":"tam","tier":0,"slot":"greeting.i-am-well","domain":1,"text_native":"நல்லா இருக்கின்றேன்","text_romanized":"nuhl-lah ih-ruk-kihn-rēhn","text_english":"I am well, thank you.","source_caption":"Fine, thank you.","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"The expected answer to the greeting above. Answering it wrong reads as evasive in cultures where it is a formula.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Tamil phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Tamil","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"tam-t0-0004","lang":"tam","tier":0,"slot":"greeting.nice-to-meet-you","domain":1,"text_native":"தங்களை சந்தித்தது மிக்க மகிழ்ச்சி","text_romanized":"thuhng-guh-luh suhn-thihth-thuh-dhu mihk-kuh muh-gizhch-chih","text_english":"Nice to meet you.","source_caption":"Nice to meet you.","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Said on a first introduction. In several languages there is a separate phrase for meeting someone formally that a stranger will use instead.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Tamil phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Tamil","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"tam-t0-0005","lang":"tam","tier":0,"slot":"greeting.what-is-your-name","domain":1,"text_native":"உங்க பெயர் என்ன?","text_romanized":"ung-guh peh-yuh-ru ehn-nuh?","text_english":"What is your name?","source_caption":"What is your name?","register":"neutral","direction":"understand","why":"You get asked this before you get to ask it. Recognising the question is the difference between answering and freezing.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Tamil phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Tamil","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"tam-t0-0006","lang":"tam","tier":0,"slot":"courtesy.please","domain":1,"text_native":"தயவு செய்து","text_romanized":"thuh-yuh-vu sey-thu","text_english":"Please.","source_caption":"Please.","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Not a filler in English, and a grammatical particle in some of these languages — one word that changes a sentence from an order to a request.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Tamil phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Tamil","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"tam-t0-0007","lang":"tam","tier":0,"slot":"courtesy.thank-you","domain":1,"text_native":"நன்றி.","text_romanized":"nuhn-drih","text_english":"Thank you.","source_caption":"Thank you.","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"The single most useful word in any of these languages. Saying it costs nothing and changes how everything after it is received.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Tamil phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Tamil","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"tam-t0-0008","lang":"tam","tier":0,"slot":"courtesy.youre-welcome","domain":1,"text_native":"நல்வரவு","text_romanized":"nuhl-vuh-ruh-vu","text_english":"You are welcome.","source_caption":"You're welcome.","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"You will be handed it constantly, and there is no way to avoid replying. In a few languages the reply is the same word as 'yes'.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Tamil phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Tamil","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"tam-t0-0009","lang":"tam","tier":0,"slot":"courtesy.excuse-me","domain":1,"text_native":"மன்னிக்கவும்","text_romanized":"muhn-nihk-kuh-vum","text_english":"Excuse me.","source_caption":"Excuse me. (getting attention)","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Two different things in one phrase: getting someone's attention, and getting past them. Guessing wrong is jarring — one version walks through a conversation.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Tamil phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Tamil","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"tam-t0-0010","lang":"tam","tier":0,"slot":"courtesy.sorry","domain":1,"text_native":"என்னை மன்னிக்கவும்","text_romanized":"ehn-nigh muhn-nihk-kuh-vum","text_english":"I am sorry.","source_caption":"I'm sorry.","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Apologising for a small fault — bumping someone, being late, not understanding. The form you use signals how much of a fault you think it was.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Tamil phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Tamil","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"tam-t0-0011","lang":"tam","tier":0,"slot":"courtesy.goodbye","domain":1,"text_native":"போய் வருகிறேன்","text_romanized":"pōhy vuh-ruh-gih-rēhn","text_english":"Goodbye.","source_caption":"Goodbye.","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"How you leave. Leaving without one is noticeably rude in most of these languages.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Tamil phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Tamil","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
